<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> In Pattern B, the number of small squares doubles from each step to the next.</item>
</list>
<para>Pattern B</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Four steps of a growing pattern. Step 0: One square. Step 1: Two squares, one atop the other. Step 2: Four squares in a two by two square. Step 3: Eight squares in a two by four rectangle."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/e1178e6969e9b4d3ddc5767534e1ad9541129430"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Write an equation to represent the number of small squares at Step \(n\) in Pattern B. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(g(n)=2^n\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="8dec6722-cdd1-46f8-890d-df530de5bd7f" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q#-->
  <exercise data-content-id="4878fa90-3d82-4e1d-98c2-47593b1e9296" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="exponential" data-solution-options="[&quot;linear&quot;, &quot;quadratic&quot;, &quot;exponential&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Is the function in Pattern B linear, quadratic, or exponential? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! It is exponential. </para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
