<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>How would the two patterns compare if they continue to grow? Make one to two observations.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The number of small squares in Pattern B grows much more quickly than the number of squares in Pattern A once
      \(n\) is greater than \(5\). The patterns have the same number of squares when \(n=2\) and when \(n=4\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
